# PTCS Dynamic shared-axis canonical event time

## Pre-work plan

- Background: Daedalus consumer verification found that shared-axis projection retains only position/value plus interval metadata; canonical `SduiTimeRow.EventTimeUtc` is lost before Renderer presentation. Interval end is not a valid substitute for completed and forming bars.
- Goal: carry optional canonical event time on the shared `TemporalAxisPoint`, preserve legacy codec compatibility, reject contradictory timestamps for the same shared position, and render completed/forming labels from producer authority.
- Scope: PTCS Dynamic RFC/current TA documents, Contracts shared-axis type/codec/validation, Renderer projection/tests, exact package graph and Daedalus handoff.
- Invariants: Renderer never infers canonical time from interval bounds; `TemporalSeriesPoint` remains position/value only; no Order/Fill domain semantics enter PTCS; legacy payloads without event time remain decodable and explicitly lack canonical timestamp authority.
- Acceptance: new encoder round-trips UTC event time; legacy v1 decode succeeds without it; contradictory same-position timestamps reject the candidate and preserve last-good state; completed `03:04` can present `03:05` only when producer supplies that canonical time, while forming preview `03:06` presents `03:06`; focused exact-package and browser gates pass.
- Risks: changing a record shape affects all exact consumers; optional legacy decode must not silently invent time; shared-axis merge must define one timestamp per position deterministically.

